  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "piecewise-introduction",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Why add piecewise inputs?\n",
    "\n",
    "The five standard NNs improve, but Run 5 still has higher RMSE than the reference GBM. Piecewise features give the NN fixed breakpoints in each numerical input. A ramp rises from 0 to 1 within its bin and stays flat outside it. The NN learns how to combine these ramps.\n",
    "\n",
    "Bin edges come from fitting-data quantiles. Scaling also uses fitting rows only. The original inputs stay in the model. This adds first-layer parameters as well as a different representation, so the effects are not separated here.\n"
   ]
  },
